      "text": "In the eighth ditch each false counsellor walks wrapped in a tongue of flame. Ulysses, who talked his crew past the edge of the world, burns in a flame with two horns. These flames can be turned with mirrors, and they light their own way. Never stand where a flame is about to go. Some eyes, once opened, stay open: counsel given can be taken back."
